    "result_text": "The full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for owner telephone numbers, rejecting mismatches with a 400.\n\n**Where the logic went** (each piece in a small, single-responsibility unit, reusing the existing E.164 pipeline):\n\n1. **`util/E164PhoneNumber.java`** \u2014 added a `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS` table (`\"1\"\u219210`, `\"61\"\u21929`) and a `hasValidNationalNumberLength(String e164)` method. This is where phone-number/E.164 domain knowledge already lives, so country-code rules belong here. It returns `true` for country codes with no known rule (so the generic 8\u201315 bound still governs them) and uses longest-prefix matching for safety.\n\n2. **`ValidateOwnerTelephoneLength`** (new pipeline step) \u2014 reads the already-normalized `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` and throws when the length is wrong. Kept separate from `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` (whose job is normalization) so each step has one responsibility.\n\n3. **`TelephoneNationalNumberLengthException`** + **handler** \u2014 a dedicated checked exception and 400 handler, matching the existing per-concern exception style (`InvalidTelephoneException`, `DuplicateTelephoneException`), reusing the shared `ProblemDetails.build` helper.\n\n4. **Wiring** \u2014 registered the escalation YAML and inserted the `validateTelephoneLength` step right after `normalizeTelephone` in both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`, so create and update behave consistently.\n\nThe new step runs after normalization (so it sees the canonical `+`-prefixed value) and before the uniqueness check. All tests pass \u2014 including the new `errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` acceptance test (`+61 123` \u2192 400) and the full suite (BUILD SUCCESS).",
